  "title": "RTCP: Strengthen heuristic",
  "description": "In the heuristic dissection, check that the reported overall length is\nat least as long as the length indicated by the 3rd and 4th octets. Only\ncheck that it's at least as long, because it could be a compound packet,\nand in SRTCP all bytes starting with the 9th are in the Encrypted\nPortion, including all the headers of subsequent packets.\n\nCommit d115cf3ca772625f96efbe63846681c7849037ee weakened the heuristic\nin order to add additional packet types for Reduced-Size RTCP; as RFC\n5506 notes, \"One potential effect of this change is much weaker validation\nthat received packets actually are RTCP and not packets of some other\ntype being wrongly delivered.  Thus, some consideration should be given\nto ensure the best possible validation is available...\" [1]\n\nCurrently the RTCP dissector does not perform close to the full header\nvalidity check for RTCP, given in RFC 3550[2], even as modified for\nRFC 5506 and Reduced-Size RTCP. This change should exclude more bogus\nnon-RTCP packets at low cost.\n\n[1] - https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc5506/#section-3.4.2\n[2] - https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc3550/#appendix-A.2",
